The release date of the official release of [i]'It came from space, and ate our brains'[/i] has been set. The game will be released on [b]19 March 2015[/b] on Steam. Make sure to add the game to your wishlist and follow our [b]community hub[/b]! Besides announcing the official release date of the game, we also released a new (beta) patch, details are listed below.

[img]http://triangle-studios.com/press/it_came_from_space_and_ate_our_brains/images/ItCameFromSpaceAndAteOurBrains_10_small.png[/img]

With all the feedback/suggestions gathered from our testers we were able to release a new patch. This patch contains several fixes and includes also some new features. Here is a list of the fixes:  

[h1]Features[/h1]
- The leaderboards are now loading correctly;
- Notification when you are able to upgrade your active weapon is now displayed correctly;
- Controller support has been extended further;
- The camera for walking down has been tweaked;
- Not only the host hears impact sounds on aliens anymore, but everyone does.  

[h1]Maps[/h1]
- Block Countryside: The water now 'streams'; 
- Block Countryside: There is now some mist in the map near the farms';
- Block Highway: It is now raining in this map; 
- Block Highway: The map now contains lightning strikes;  
- Block Hospital: The lightning around the fountain the middle has been increased;
- Black Crash Site: The lightning around the UFO has been increased; 
- Block City: There are now small burning papers flying around the map; 
- Block Planet: More floating objects in the map;  
- All maps now contain a bit more fire and smoke particles.    

[h1]Enemies[/h1]
- Dodgers don't get stuck in walls anymore; 
- Forcers don't get stuck in walls anymore.   

[h1]Weapons[/h1]
- Particles left-overs from weapons are not displayed anymore.  

